   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the value of \\( \\lim_{x \\to 5} \\frac{\\sqrt{x + 4} - 3}{x - 5} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         1,
         6
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x + 4 \\). As \\( x \\to 5 \\), \\( u \\to 9 \\), and \\( x - 5 = u - 9 \\), so the numerator is \\( g(u) - g(9) \\) with \\( g(u) = \\sqrt{u} \\) and \\( g(9) = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( g(u) = \\sqrt{u} \\) and the base point is \\( u = 9 \\).",
         "mathjson": 9
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is \\( \\lim_{u \\to 9} \\frac{g(u) - g(9)}{u - 9} = g'(9) \\), and \\( g'(u) = \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{u}} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
